  "user_id": 18603,
  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "##Representing Input and Output with Flowcharts\r\n\r\n1. Explore the flowchart provided in the sketch on this level. Note any patterns you see repeated on the \"Order Cake\" branch and \"Order Cupcakes\" branch.\r\n2. Name the repeated inputs and replace them with a single function.\r\n3. Complete the two different user paths from start to end by filling in the green boxes. Then come up with a descriptive name for the function that takes in these two inputs.\r\n\r\n:::details [What's a user path?]\r\nThink about how what inputs you would need to represent a specific cake. For example, how would you model a user ordering a **Large Chocolate Fudge Cake that says \"Happy Birthday\"**?\r\n:::\r\n",
